Bugfix: Large web uploads survive a single failed chunk and name the cause

A chunked upload in the web interface of a logged-in user was abandoned as a
whole as soon as one chunk request failed - a 44 GB file is about 4,400
chunks, so a single proxy timeout or PHP-FPM restart during hours of uploading
was enough. Transient failures (no response, 408, 429 and 5xx except 501/507)
now go through the same resume path as a stalled upload: the chunks already on
the server are listed and the upload continues from there, with pauses of
5, 10 and 15 seconds. Making progress since the last failure restores the full
number of retries.

The error message now names the HTTP status. Under HTTP/2 there is no status
text and jQuery only reports "error", which hid whether a proxy answered with
413, 502 or 504. Upload messages are no longer escaped twice, so quotes and
ampersands in file names show up as such instead of &quot; and &amp;.
